.policy "ruff-c411-unnecessary-list-call" revision 3
.description "Remove the list call around a list comprehension; the comprehension already builds a new list."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff C411 (flake8-comprehensions): `list(…)` of the builtin list (by name), whose one argument is a list
// comprehension; in the file and in string type definitions. Its fix is unsafe; none here.
//   list([f(x) for x in y])    ← C411: [f(x) for x in y]
//   list(f(x) for x in y)      not reported here (C400)
#include "python/python-15.rerail"
//   lookup_call(c, x), lookup_str_call(c, x), lookup_only(c, a); c4_comp(e, k) (python/comprehensions)

.violation C411(at: node) code "C411"
    "Remove the outer `list()` call and keep the list comprehension; it already builds a new list."
    suppress ruff "C411"
C411(c) :- (lookup_call(c, "list") ; lookup_str_call(c, "list")), lookup_only(c, l), c4_comp(l, "list").
lookup_name("list").
